            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Arabic for to punish, then the Arabic for to inform the police."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: للمرة الأولى",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "للمرة الأولى — li-l-marra al-ūlā — \"for the first time\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "رأيت البحر للمرة الأولى في حياتي. raʾaytu al-baḥr li-l-marra al-ūlā fī ḥayātī. I saw the sea for the first time in my life."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also لأول مرة."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "للمرة الأولى (li-l-marra al-ūlā) is \"for the first passing\": marra is built on the native Arabic root m-r-r, \"to pass\" (Lane), and ūlā is the feminine of awwal, first."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
